WEBVTT

00:00:00.550 --> 00:00:04.340
Security analysts often begin investigations inside a SIEM platform.

00:00:04.340 --> 00:00:08.905
They review alerts, search logs, build timelines, identify affected users or systems,

00:00:08.905 --> 00:00:11.390
and determine whether activity is benign or malicious.

00:00:11.390 --> 00:00:15.446
A SIEM helps analysts move from a single alert to a broader picture of what happened.

00:00:15.446 --> 00:00:19.280
SIEM platforms support threat hunting, incident response, compliance reporting,

00:00:19.280 --> 00:00:21.060
and operational monitoring.

00:00:21.060 --> 00:00:24.750
Analysts may pivot from one event to related information, such as user logins,

00:00:24.750 --> 00:00:28.923
endpoint activity, network connections, cloud changes, or application logs.

00:00:28.923 --> 00:00:30.140
SIEM is not the entire SOC,

00:00:30.140 --> 00:00:34.280
but it is frequently one of the central tools analysts use during daily operations.

00:00:34.280 --> 00:00:36.620
It works best when analysts understand the environment,

00:00:36.620 --> 00:00:38.570
know what good and bad activity can look like,

00:00:38.570 --> 00:00:40.740
and keep detections aligned with current risks.
